  "evidence": "TEXT_D: 40,000 more frontline police with zero tolerance and tougher sentencing; freeze non‑essential immigration, stop the boats, Leave ECHR, prioritise locals for social housing; patriotic curriculum and celebration of national days; make work pay via higher tax thresholds, stricter benefits (two‑strike rule), lower business taxes, looser hiring/firing; NHS zero waiting lists using independent capacity and tax relief; restore sovereignty, British Bill of Rights.\nTEXT_C: Rebuild a fully public NHS, free personal care, major anti‑poverty uplifts and path to UBI; wealth tax, 10:1 pay ratios, rent controls and ending Right to Buy; humane asylum with safe routes and ending the hostile environment; end new oil and gas, rising carbon tax, Clean Air Act, extensive nature/animal protections; proportional representation and curbing big money; path to rejoin the EU, cancel Trident, reform NATO toward de‑escalation.",
  "reasoning": "Given a profile that weights authority and proportionality slightly more than equality and sanctity, TEXT_D aligns by stressing law‑and‑order, national sovereignty and loyalty, and merit‑ and work‑rewarding policies while still addressing care via NHS access. TEXT_C emphasizes equality and environmental purity and often challenges traditional authority and national loyalty, making it a weaker fit for the stated priorities.",
